<title>INDIA: TABLE-India ONGC 96/97 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-India ONGC 96/97 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>		(in billion rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     20.34  vs   19.45</p>
<p>    Net sales	     132.48  vs  131.06</p>
<p>    Div (pct)		20     vs   20</p>
<p>    Other income	    6.11  vs    6.11</p>
<p>    Total expenditure    72.97  vs   73.80</p>
<p>    Interest		  8.67  vs    9.66</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   31.62  vs   32.48</p>
<p>    Tax			 4.99  vs    4.09</p>
<p>NOTE: Oil and Natural Gas Corp Ltd said in a statement that depreciation included depletion and amortisation.</p>
<p>It said the profit in 1996/97 was not fully represented by cash accruals since the receivables had gone up by 23.15 billion rupees as on March 31 1997 compared with the previous years, due to non-receipt of some dues from oil coordination committee and oil companies.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
